<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">My Western Home (The Kirwin Chief)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1874</span><span class="sg-chain-h">republication of the poem</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">A Home on the Range (in John Lomax, Cowboy Songs and Other Frontier Ballads)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1910</span><span class="sg-chain-h">collected version</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Arrangement by David W. Guion (G. Schirmer)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1925</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sheet music arrangement</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Bing Crosby with Lennie Hayton and his orchestra</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1933</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Frank Sinatra</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1946</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Range Rider</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1950s</span><span class="sg-chain-h">television theme</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Oily Hare (Bugs Bunny)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1952</span><span class="sg-chain-h">parody words about Texas oilmen</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Rescuers Down Under</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1990</span><span class="sg-chain-h">parody sung by a villain</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Kansas, The Prelude Implicit</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2016</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li></ul></section>
